# Architecture Principles (read first, every session)

Authoritative spec: `docs/tech-architecture-requirements.md`. Quick rules below.

## Layers (strict, top → bottom only)

```
Router (app/api/**)  →  Service (app/services/**)  →  Repository (app/repositories/**)  →  DB
                                          ↓
                              Integration / Adapter (app/integrations/**)
```

**Hard import rules — review-rejecting:**

- Router NEVER imports `app.repositories.*`, `app.integrations.*`, or `app.workers.*`.
- Service NEVER imports `fastapi.*`, `Request`, `Response`, or raises `HTTPException`.
- Repository NEVER calls `.commit()` and never calls another repository; cross-aggregate orchestration belongs in services.
- Integration NEVER imports services or repositories.
- User-visible strings are NEVER hardcoded — they go through `Translator` / `_("key")`. See `i18n-l10n.mdc`.
- Locale lives at the **rendering boundary** (router / listener / template), never in domain/business logic. No `if locale == "ar":` in services.

## SOLID (project-specific)

- **S** — One responsibility per class/module: routers do HTTP, services do business, repos do persistence.
- **O** — Extend via new `Protocol` implementation; do not edit existing concrete classes.
- **L** — Every implementation of a `Protocol` passes the same contract test suite.
- **I** — Split protocols by capability (`Reader`, `Writer`, `HealthCheck`) over a fat interface.
- **D** — Services depend on `Protocol`s, never on concrete classes; wiring lives in `app/core/container.py`.

## DRY / KISS / YAGNI

- **DRY:** extract only after the **third** occurrence; prefer duplication over the wrong abstraction.
- **KISS:** no metaclasses, no clever decorators, no magic. Prefer obvious code.
- **YAGNI:** no empty interfaces "for later", no plugin systems with one plugin, no config knobs without a current user.

## DI (FastAPI-native, no third-party container)

- Composition root: `app/core/container.py` holds `get_*` factory functions.
- Routers use `Depends(get_*_service)`. Services receive collaborators via `__init__`.
- Every dep MUST be overridable via `app.dependency_overrides` for tests.
- No `lru_cache` on per-request-state functions (sessions, request scope).

## Engineering checklist (every PR)

- Type-annotate everything; mypy strict.
- Async all the way down (no `requests`, no sync DB).
- No magic strings/numbers — use `app/core/constants.py`.
- No `if APP_ENV == "test":` in business code.
- No commented-out code; no TODOs without a ticket ID.
- Any new user-visible string is added to `messages.pot` in the same PR (`make i18n-extract && make i18n-update`); both `en` and `ar` catalogs translated before merge.

## When unsure

Default to **simpler**, **more explicit**, **fewer abstractions**. If a `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` rule conflicts with generic best practice, the rule wins.
